      "summary": "Describes an externally owned Direct3D 12 device and its native queue configuration.",
      "details": "Describes an externally owned Direct3D 12 device and its native queue configuration. All native pointers are non-owning and must remain valid through backend shutdown. The native backend retains COM references to the supplied device and queues, but Arda never destroys the host-owned native device. External presentation is not supported by the current wrapper; the host should import frame images and manage presentation.",
